WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
Hang a uniform rod from one end.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.380
Beside it, hang a ball on a
string of the same length.

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.690
Set both swinging gently.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.930
The ball takes 2.0 seconds
for each complete swing.

5
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.690
The rod takes only 1.6.

6
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:21.090
Add a block bouncing on a spring, and a
flat wheel twisting to and fro on a wire.

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.300
Why do such different systems
all oscillate in the same way?

8
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.640
In this mission, you'll apply Newton's
second law to a block on a spring,

9
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.290
and find the pattern its motion obeys.

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.330
Then you'll swing rigid bodies,
twist a body hanging on a wire,

11
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.330
and work out their periods.

12
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.370
Your mission: explain why such different
systems all oscillate in exactly the

13
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:44.280
same way.
